course: dictionary
lesson: 3945
title: Fume, fumes and fuming
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word fume has two main meanings, and the clues in the sentence tell you which one is meant. Fumes are smoke, gas or strong smells that are harmful to breathe. «Use model paint and glue in a ventilated place, because fumes can make you feel ill.» Here the fumes are the harmful smells from paint and glue, so you need fresh air.
explain: The other meaning is about feelings. «She fumed all the way home.» Nobody is breathing smoke here. She was very angry and kept it inside, probably quietly grumbling to herself. Ask yourself: is this about air and smells, or about feelings? The words around it give the clue.
explain: Cars can give out fumes too. «Smog is a dirty haze of smoke and car fumes that builds up in still air.» Try swapping in "smoke and gas" and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does, so fumes means smoke or gas here. Always check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Fumes are smoke, gas or strong smells that are unpleasant or harmful to breathe.
fact: To fume is to be very angry, often quietly or while waiting.
fact: To fume can also mean to give off smoke or gas.
fact: «I'm fuming» means I'm really angry. This is informal, mostly used in the UK.
fact: Useful phrases: «exhaust fumes», «paint fumes», «toxic fumes», and «running on fumes», which means almost out of fuel or energy.
exercise: «Use model paint and glue in a ventilated place, because fumes can make you feel ill.» What are fumes here? | Loud noises from a workshop | Sweet smells from baking | *Smoke, gas or strong smells that are harmful to breathe | Small pieces of paper
exercise: «She fumed all the way home.» What does fumed mean? | Laughed loudly all the way | Ran very fast | Gave off a sweet smell | *Was very angry, quietly and for a long time
exercise: «Smog is a dirty haze of smoke and car fumes.» What are car fumes? | A bright, sunny sky | The sound of a horn | *Smoke and gas given out by a car's engine | Clean air from a open window
test: Someone says «I'm fuming» in the UK. What do they mean? | I'm very tired and want to sleep | I'm feeling cold after the rain | I'm lost on the way home | *I'm really angry
test: Before you paint at home, what is a safe thing to do? | *Open a window so fresh air can flow through | Put the paint close to a fire | Shut all the windows and doors | Breathe in the paint fumes deeply
exam: What does «running on fumes» mean? | Running very fast with smoke behind | Being given a brand new car | Playing outside in the rain | *Almost out of fuel or energy
